      "problem": "Calculate the value of $2+ (-6).$",
      "worked_solution": "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give \n\n$$\n2+ (-6) = 2-6.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we move $6$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149424/assets/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nWe end up at $-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n2 + (-6) = -4.\n$$",
